A||N||7||Seanh||3.4 or S/C 3800?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||09-29-2000||08:20 PM||||I decided to ask this after reading another thread. I am rebuilding my 86GT, not the engine, the entire car. I need to do a conprssion check, but I am not planning on doing an engine rebuild at this time. I have been hearing that a 3.4 or 3800 are fairly reasonably priced. I was wondering, what are the pro's and con's of each engine, which is going to give me the best performance for the money? What car do these engines come out of? How long would it take to do this engine conversion alone? Also, what is the HP of both these engines?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-29-2000||09:02 PM||||The 3.4 is probably easier than the 3.8 because you do not need to do a lot of rewiring for the 3.8 conversion.  Out of the box a 3.4 will give you a min of 160 hp and 210 ft lbs of torque.  The 3.8 would give you a min of  190 hp. Either engine can be built up to however deep your pocket is.  <P>If you go for a professional rebuild plan on $3-4K  for the 3.4 and $6-8 K for the 3.8. Depending on engine cost.  (I guess if I were redoing a car I wouldn't stick a $200 engine in it).<P>You can get brand new 3.4 from GM or something from the GM minivans are supposed to be the easiest swap doner car.  The 3.8s come from Buicks or Pontiacs.  The 3.8 hp ratings will vary depending on which year the engine is.   The 3.8 s/c has 240 hp.<P>If you check the web sites of Ed Parks, Bob Steiger, Chris West etc, they should have some prices down for the swaps.  These are some of the reputable Fiero repair shops I've heard of.  There are others.<P>Determine what you'll want the car for.  A tire burning screamer will be expensive and not last long.  But if you have deep pockets or the skill and time to do the repairs you can get anything you want.<P><BR>Time for the engine swap depends on your skill and what else has to be fixed or replaced. ||||reg||2
Z||000002||Seanh||09-29-2000||09:20 PM||||I currently do a little street racing now, but I am usally burned most of the time. I was wondering, you said the 3.4 puts out about 160 hp min. If I build my current 2.8 up to a 3.1 iv heard it will do about 165  hp and Iv been told they can be built up to do about 190-210 hp with a more aggressive cam. Would I be better off to do that? I would really like to have a 3800S/C but I dont alot of time to work on it if I have problems with a more powerful engine. I am planning on doing it myself. How much trouble would I have with a 3800S/C? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||09-29-2000||11:41 PM||||Where does one find a clutch that'll live behind a high torque motor in our cars?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-30-2000||05:11 AM||||Seanh:  The degree of difficulty would depend on your skill level.  The most difficult thing for the 3800 swap as I understand it is the mating of the 3800 wiring harness from the engine to the stock wiring harness of the Fiero.  The second may be axles, clutch or transmission set up.<P>Phil has had no problems with his 3800 s/c, but his was built by ACE.  If you had the $10-11K you may be able to purchase a completed car.  A little more and V8 Archie would have a ready made car with his V8 engine.<P>You may build up the 2.8 engine however you want, to get the maximum power from it.  Remember that as the HP goes up for a 2.8, life expectency goes down.<P>Professional drag racers get 5-10 quarter mile races in with their engines, (if they are lucky) before the engines break or need a rebuild.  So if you build a 2.8 to 200 or 300 HP don't expect to be driving it a long time.  Or expect to do frequent rebuilds.<P>However you reconstruct the Fiero is your personal preference depending on your wallet.  There are too many options avaialable. Cams, pistons. injectors, turbos, s/c, NOS, fuel rails, throttle bodies, carburators...... and the list goes on. Remeber that there will always be someone faster out there who have had a deeper pocket to build a faster car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||09-30-2000||11:44 PM||||If I were to build up my 2.8 to get maybe 200 hp, how far down the line could I expect to have trouble with it? I dont really dive fast, or race alot, but would they life of my engine go down even if I built it up and only pushed it occasionally? Do you know of a good source for 2.8 v6 engine blocks? or do these come with the rebuild kits? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000006||RobertVol||10-01-2000||01:19 AM||||It is true the most difficult thing with the 3800 conversion is the wiring setup. The engine does not cause much weight differential problems. and the mating to an automatic is not a prob either. It gets a little trickier on the Sticks. Mine is a stick and there were some adapting problems and had a slight problem with gear assigment but I wouldnt trade the performance of my SC' engine for the 3.4 anyday. It will cost a little more but as everyone knows.....<P>HP = $$$$$ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Like Phil mine was done by ACE and I spent a little more but I have been REALLY HAPPY! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||10-01-2000||08:11 AM||||Try emailing BENGAL4.  He just got his back from the FieroFactory (something like that) in Toronto.  Seems to me that he's got the Getrag, so he could tell you of any problems.  I know that he spent alot of money on his, but if you have the cash, more power to you (pun intended).  Personally, I can't afford the cost so I'll end up with a stout 3.4 for less than 1/2 the cost.  I don't plan on gassing on it often, but I want to make sure I have a little extra power on tap in case I get stoplighted by a riced Yugo <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Best of luck, whatever you decide.||||reg||1
